            <ArticleTitle>Physical Activity as Cause and Cure of Muscular Pain: Evidence of Underlying Mechanisms.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>136-145</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1249/JES.0000000000000112</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Work-related physical activity (PA), in terms of peak loads and sustained and/or repetitive contractions, presents risk factors for the development of muscular pain and disorders. However, PA as a training tailored to the employee's work exposure, health, and physical capacity offers prevention and rehabilitation. We suggest the concept of &quot;Intelligent Physical Exercise Training&quot; relying on evidence-based sports science training principles.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
